## Part 2: Deterministic vs. LLM Classification Table

| Failure Mode | Domain | Deterministic Logic | LLM Judge Needed? | Cheap Assertions |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FM-SE-001 (Double-Spend) | Settlement | No—needs reconciliation exec | YES (Settlement) | Amount match, CBDC commit flag |
| FM-SE-002 (Batch Mismatch) | Settlement | Batch sum = order sum (arithmetic) | YES (Settlement) | Sum comparison, no duplicates |
| FM-SE-003 (Netting Overflow) | Settlement | Detect int64 overflow | MAYBE | `settlements > math.MaxInt64` |
| FM-SE-004 (Ledger Inconsistency) | Settlement | Verify ledger balance reads | YES (Settlement) | Before/after balance snapshot |
| FM-CO-001 (KYC Failed) | Compliance | KYC status field = "verified" | YES (Compliance) | Simple string comparison first |
| FM-CO-002 (Velocity Exceeded) | Compliance | `current_velocity > threshold` | YES (Compliance) | Numeric comparison only |
| FM-CO-003 (Sanctions Match) | Compliance | Sanctions list age, threshold | YES (Compliance) | Age seconds, match score |
| FM-OR-001 (Invalid Transition) | Orchestration | Allowed state graph check | YES (Orchestration) | Graph membership lookup |
| FM-OR-002 (Wrong Order) | Orchestration | Step sequence validation | YES (Orchestration) | Order position check |
| FM-LA-001 (Hash Chain Broken) | Lineage | **DETERMINISTIC** (SHA256 verify) | NO—pure crypto | Compute expected hash |
| FM-LA-002 (Timestamps) | Lineage | **DETERMINISTIC** (strictly increasing) | NO—pure logic | Pairwise timestamp compare |
| FM-LA-003 (Missing Fields) | Lineage | **DETERMINISTIC** (field presence) | NO—pure logic | Non-empty checks |

### Key Insight

**3 failure modes are purely deterministic** (no LLM needed):
- FM-LA-001: Hash chain validation (crypto proof)
- FM-LA-002: Timestamp monotonicity (ordering)
- FM-LA-003: Required field presence (schema)

These can be scored inline via LineageJudge (which already does this—see `lineage_judge.go:41-56`).

**All others require LLM judge** to assess nuance (e.g., reconciliation result interpretation, compliance context, workflow intent).

