## Part 6: Honest CI Floor Approach

### Gate 1: Offline (make eval)
```
Requirement: passRate ≥ 85% on all 55+ cases
Judges:      MockSettlementJudge, MockComplianceJudge, MockOrchestrationJudge, MockLineageJudge
Logic:       Deterministic rules only (no LLM)
Time:        ~200ms
Failure:     Blocks merge to main
```

### Gate 2: Nightly LLM Calibration (TestJudgeAccuracy_OnTestSet)
```
Requirement: For each judge (Settlement, Compliance, Orchestration, Lineage):
             TPR_lowerBound(95% CI) ≥ 0.90  AND
             TNR_lowerBound(95% CI) ≥ 0.90

             If any judge fails → alert ops team, do NOT block main merge
             (true judges take time to calibrate; offline gate is primary blocker)

Judges:      Real LLM-based judges (SettlementJudge, etc.)
Data:        40% test split of GoldenDataset
Time:        ~5-10 min (nightly cron @ 2 AM)
Failure:     Alert + historical trend tracking (no CI block)
```

### Metrics Reported

Each nightly calibration reports:
- Judge name (Settlement, Compliance, Orchestration, Lineage)
- TPR and 95% CI bounds
- TNR and 95% CI bounds
- Optimal threshold (for future fine-tuning)
- Sample count (# ground-truth cases used)

