## Part 8: Key Contracts & Design Principles

| Contract | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **1 Case = 1 Truth** | Golden cases have single ground-truth expectation; no pre-baked `actual_output` |
| **Real Execution** | Judge routes to genuine validation logic—no mocks that always pass |
| **Dispatch by Domain** | Failure mode FM-DOMAIN-NNN parsed to select appropriate judge |
| **Deterministic First** | `make eval` runs fast with mocks; nightly runs LLM for calibration only |
| **Honest Metrics** | TPR/TNR reported with 95% CI bounds; lower bounds define gate |
| **Judge Lifecycle** | Mock judges for CI; real judges for calibration; separate concerns |
| **Input Parity** | Case Input/Expected maps directly to judge's input struct via constructors |
| **Failure as Data** | Judges return Verdict{Pass, Score, Reason, Evidence}; no silent failures |

